    "https://jobs.roosevelt.edu/postings/8930": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Roosevelt University Employment Opportunities | Campus Safety Officer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Users Returning Users Campus Safety Officer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Campus Safety Officer Category Campus Safety Position Number Posting Number S0001406 Location Chicago Open Date 10/07/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? No Job Type Full-Time Working Hours Position Summary The Campus Safety Officer is responsible for ensuring the security and safety of all students, employees and visitors on the University Campus. Roosevelt University seeks a full-time Campus Safety Officer at the Chicago Campus for the midnight shift (10:30PM-7:00AM). This is a union position and will require union membership; health and wellness benefits is provided by the union. The salary for this position is $19.75/hr. Title IX Contact Information: Federal Title IX policy requires that all colleges and universities make known the contact information for the person responsible for coordinating its efforts to comply with Title IX regulations. At Roosevelt University, the Title IX Coordinator is Natasha Robinson. Her office is located in the Auditorium Building of the Chicago campus, 430 S. Michigan Avenue, AUD 476B. She can be reached at 312-281-3245 or TitleIX@roosevelt.edu. Do not contact this email address for inquiries about your job application; if you have questions, you may email hrquestions@roosevelt.edu . Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required Minimum 2 years of relevant experience. Demonstrated ability to exercise considerable judgment, discretion and professionalism in managing sensitive situations and/or irate individuals. Excellent organizational, communication (written and verbal), interpersonal skills, observation and attention to detail. Ability to demonstrate a commitment to service excellence by embodying Roosevelt’s core values, mission, and vision in every aspect of the role working with students, faculty, staff, and visitors. A positive and professional demeanor is a must. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite including Word, Excel, and Outlook. Years of Experience Required 2 Required Education High School/GED Certification/Licensure Required Minimum Qualifications Please refer to knowledge, skills, and abilities required. Preferred Qualifications Earned Associate’s or Bachelor’s Degree in Criminal Justice or related field. One year continuous security/safety experience. Previous experience in preliminary investigation and preparing incident reports. Previous customer service experience. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite including Word, Excel, Outlook. Previous experience in higher education. Equipment Operated Basic office equipment (desktop computer, copier/ multi-function device, fax and telephone), two-way radio. Security video management systems; electronic access systems; visitor management systems. Vehicle. Working Conditions May be exposed to inclement weather and extremes of temperature. May be exposed to high levels of noise – ex., fire alarms, sirens. May be exposed to dangers inherent in working in a security and safety role. Normal climate-controlled office environment is provided. Job is largely sedentary, but there is a need to move about the office and buildings frequently. Occasional bending, stooping, lifting, pushing and/or pulling is required (typically less than 10 pounds of weight or pressure). Regular use of desktop computer is required, calling for frequent hand/wrist movement and repetition. Moderate level of stress. Occasional travel within the local or regional setting may be required. Priority Application Instructions Departmental Contact Information Essential Job Functions Duty and Responsibility Secure campus and facilities by: patrolling interior and exterior of buildings and campus; locking/unlocking doors; observing for and following up on suspicious persons/circumstances; responding to various security and safety related incidents; checking and inspecting building, security, fire and life safety equipment. Percentage Of Time 40 Duty and Responsibility Ensures ongoing coverage at all security posts; monitor people as they enter and exit; greet, check identification, issue guest badges, keys, and respond to student, staff and visitor inquiries. Enforce Roosevelt rules & regulations. Monitor and respond to building, security, fire and life safety equipment/systems. Percentage Of Time 40 Duty and Responsibility Conducts preliminary investigations and prepares incident reports recording observations, information, occurrences, statements and/or surveillance activities; updates a daily activity and other reports in accordance with department’s policies and procedures. Percentage Of Time 10 Duty and Responsibility Participates in ongoing compliance, training and various emergency preparedness activities. Percentage Of Time 5 Duty and Responsibility Other duties as assigned. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned High School Diploma or GED? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have in a similar role? (Open Ended Question) Will you now or at any point in the future require employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) to legally work in the United States? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents 430 S. Michigan, Chicago, IL To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.roosevelt.edu/postings/8923": {
      "title": "Artist-Teacher of Musical Theatre Voice",
      "description": "Roosevelt University Employment Opportunities | Artist-Teacher of Musical Theatre Voice Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Users Returning Users Artist-Teacher of Musical Theatre Voice Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Rank Artist Teacher of Musical Theatre Voice – Part Time Track Non-Tenure Track Position Title Artist-Teacher of Musical Theatre Voice Category Part-Time Faculty Position Number Posting Number F0000278 Location Chicago Open Date 10/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Job Type Part-Time Working Hours Position Summary Reflecting the ideals of its founders in 1945, Roosevelt University is a private, nonsectarian community of educators, scholars and learners committed to academic, creative and service excellence, who value differences in personal experiences and perspectives, ask difficult questions, and promote mutual understanding, inclusion, social consciousness and action toward social justice. Recognizing that difference broadens perspectives, Roosevelt University seeks and serves a diverse, promising student body from metropolitan Chicago and around the world. We invite you to contribute your talents to our community. The Chicago College of Performing Arts ( CCPA ) at Roosevelt is comprised of three Conservatories: Music, Interdisciplinary Studies, and Theatre. Our faculty and staff maintain successful professional careers in their chosen fields alongside their commitment to training and educating our students in preparation to enter performing arts industries. Please note that there are multiple openings for this position. Job Duties: Teach weekly private lessons to undergraduate Musical Theater majors and other students on degree tracks within the Theatre Conservatory that include voice. Actively recruit potential students Sustain a successful studio through effective, and healthy pedagogy. Participate in program activities including adjudication of juries and program auditions The pay for this position is $70/hr. Title IX Contact Information: Federal Title IX policy requires that all colleges and universities make known the contact information for the person responsible for coordinating its efforts to comply with Title IX regulations. At Roosevelt University, the Title IX Coordinator is Natasha Robinson. Her office is located in the Auditorium Building of the Chicago campus, 430 S. Michigan Avenue, AUD 476B. She can be reached at 312-281-3245 or TitleIX@roosevelt.edu. Do not contact this email address for inquiries about your job application; if you have questions, you may email hrquestions@roosevelt.edu . Special Instructions Summary Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required Bachelor’s degree required; Significant documented teaching and/or performing experience will be considered in place of earned degrees. Documented record of professional experience and visibility as a performer required. Functional piano skills to support a voice lesson required. Experience in repertoire ranging from pre-Golden Age to contemporary pop/rock styles. Both generalists and specialists who demonstrate a willingness to collaborate across styles and approaches will be considered. Background in pedagogy and vocal health, strong knowledge of IPA , CCM , crossover repertoire, amplified singing, vocal improvisation, and body work are all of interest. Documented success in collegiate teaching preferred. Years of Experience Required 1-2 years teaching at the university level Certification/Licensure Required Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 1-2 years teaching performers at the college level. Significant documented teaching and/or performing experience will be considered in place of earned degrees. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Equipment Operated Studio sound system, basic office/ classroom equipment and Smart-classroom equipment (computer, monitor, projector and audio equipment). Working Conditions Standard climate controlled office and classroom environment. Priority Application Instructions Departmental Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have an earned Bachelors degree? Yes No Do you have at least 1-2 years teaching at the university level? (Open Ended Question) Will you now or at any point in the future require employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) to legally work in the United States? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter List of References Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents 430 S. Michigan, Chicago, IL To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.roosevelt.edu/postings/8915": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer (Goalkeeping)",
      "description": "Roosevelt University Employment Opportunities | Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer (Goalkeeping) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Users Returning Users Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer (Goalkeeping) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer (Goalkeeping) Category Administrative Position Number Posting Number S0001403 Location Hybrid - Chicago Open Date 10/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? No Job Type Part-Time Working Hours Position Summary The Assistant Coach, Women’s Soccer will aid the head coach in providing position specific skill instruction and student-athlete support to goal keepers in compliance with all institutional, NCAA and Great Lakes Intercollegiate Athletic Conference ( GLIAC ) rules and regulations. Duties of the role will include goal-keeper practice planning and assessment, student-athlete instruction and evaluation during practice and competition, and supporting the head coach in recruitment of prospective student-athletes. This is a part-time, administrative, exempt, position that reports to the Associate Athletic Director/Head Coach, Women’s Soccer. The salary range for this position is $8,000-$9,000. Title IX Contact Information: Federal Title IX policy requires that all colleges and universities make known the contact information for the person responsible for coordinating its efforts to comply with Title IX regulations. At Roosevelt University, the Title IX Coordinator is Natasha Robinson. Her office is located in the Auditorium Building of the Chicago campus, 430 S. Michigan Avenue, AUD 476B. She can be reached at 312-281-3245 or TitleIX@roosevelt.edu. Do not contact this email address for inquiries about your job application; if you have questions, you may email hrquestions@roosevelt.edu . Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required Prior experience in assigned program as a coach, participant or related role Excellent organizational, communication (written and verbal), interpersonal skills and attention to detail Ability to exercise considerable judgment and discretion in establishing and maintaining good working relationships Ability to demonstrate a commitment to service excellence by embodying Roosevelt’s core values, mission, and vision in every aspect of the role working with students, faculty, staff, and visitors A positive and professional demeanor is a must Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite including Word, Excel, and Outlook Years of Experience Required 0-2 Required Education Bachelor's Degree Certification/Licensure Required Minimum Qualifications Please refer to Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities required. Preferred Qualifications Prior recruiting experience at the college level Prior coaching experience at the college level Equipment Operated Basic office equipment (desktop computer, copier/ multi-function device, fax and telephone). Working Conditions The assistant coach will work in multiple environments, indoors and outdoors, including areas for team practice, competition and recruiting, in addition to an office setting. The schedule will include nights and weekends and travel with the team for competitions, as well as for prospective student recruitment and other duties as assigned. Priority Application Instructions Departmental Contact Information Essential Job Functions Duty and Responsibility Competition and Practice Management: Aid the head coach in facilitating goal keeper instruction during team practices and competitions providing real-time feedback to student-athletes to instruct and motivate to improve their skill-set. Ensure student-athlete safety and welfare during practices and competitions. Occasionally assist with team travel to competitions. Percentage Of Time 70 Duty and Responsibility Practice Planning and Assessment: Provide post-practice assessment to gauge individual student-athlete and team progress towards established goals. Assist Head Coach with development of strategies for installment during practices and execution during scheduled competitions. Percentage Of Time 25 Duty and Responsibility Student-Athlete Recruitment: Aid the Head Coach, as needed, in the recruitment of prospective student-athletes, including on-campus visits, occasional off-campus events and on-going dialogue that drives enrollment. Percentage Of Time 25 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's Degree in a relevant field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of 1 year of experience working as a coach or as a former student-athlete? Yes No Will you now or at any point in the future require employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) to legally work in the United States? Yes No This is a hybrid position. Do you have the ability to work on the Chicago campus 3 days per week and attend any other in-person events as required? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents 430 S. Michigan, Chicago, IL To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
