    "https://jobs.roosevelt.edu/postings/8898": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Financial Aid Systems",
      "description": "Roosevelt University Employment Opportunities | Associate Director, Financial Aid Systems Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Users Returning Users Associate Director, Financial Aid Systems Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Associate Director, Financial Aid Systems Category Administrative Position Number A99794 Posting Number S0001397 Location Hybrid - Chicago/Schaumburg Open Date 09/17/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Job Type Full-Time Working Hours Position Summary Roosevelt University Financial Aid Services is seeking an Associate Director of Financial Aid Systems within the Office of Financial Aid Services. The Office of Financial Aid Services administers financial aid for Roosevelt University’s undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral students and plays a critical role in supporting student access, success, and institutional enrollment goals. The Associate Director of Financial Aid Systems is responsible for the hands-on administration and continuous improvement of the University’s Banner Financial Aid module and related financial aid technologies. This position serves as the lead technical expert for Banner Financial Aid and manages system setup, configuration, upgrades, testing, troubleshooting, integrations, reporting, and compliance-related processes. The Associate Director works collaboratively with Financial Aid, Enrollment Management, Information Technology, Student Accounts, and external agencies to ensure accurate financial aid processing, data integrity, regulatory compliance, and efficient system performance. The role also leads reporting and analytics efforts, develops process automation solutions, and drives technology enhancements that improve service delivery, support enrollment objectives, and strengthen the student experience. This position may be based at either Roosevelt University’s Chicago or Schaumburg campus. It is a hybrid position, requiring on‑campus presence a minimum of three days per week. Please note that remote work is possible in the following states: AZ CA IL IN FL MN NC NE NY SC SD WA WI Why Join Roosevelt University: This role offers an opportunity to shape the future of financial aid technology at an institution committed to student access, service excellence, and continuous improvement. The Associate Director will play a central role in modernizing systems, strengthening data informed decision making, and enhancing the student experience in a collaborative, enrollment‑focused environment. Roosevelt University offers many great benefits. Please review our benefits in further detail by clicking this link: https://rooseveltu.touchpointsonline.com/ The salary range for this position is $85,000-$88,000 Title IX Contact Information: Federal Title IX policy requires that all colleges and universities make known the contact information for the person responsible for coordinating its efforts to comply with Title IX regulations. At Roosevelt University, the Title IX Coordinator is Natasha Robinson. Her office is located in the Auditorium Building of the Chicago campus, 430 S. Michigan Avenue, AUD 476B. She can be reached at 312-281-3245 or TitleIX@roosevelt.edu. Do not contact this email address for inquiries about your job application; if you have questions, you may email hrquestions@roosevelt.edu . Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required Bachelor’s degree. Minimum of five years of experience administering or supporting Ellucian Banner Experience with databases, reporting tools, and emerging technologies within higher education. Years of Experience Required 5 Required Education Bachelor's Degree Certification/Licensure Required Minimum Qualifications Please see Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required section. Preferred Qualifications Understanding of data governance, data definitions, classifications, and sensitivity of information. Demonstrated project management skills, including experience supporting system implementations, conversions, or major upgrades. Strong analytical skills with a demonstrated commitment to data integrity and validation in complex systems. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with a strong customer service orientation and experience working with diverse stakeholders. Programming and data integration experience. Experience providing administrative or programmatic support within an enrollment, financial aid, or student services context Equipment Operated Office equipment (desktop computer, laptop, office copier/printer Working Conditions Normal climate-controlled office environment is provided. Job is largely sedentary, but there is a need to move about the office and buildings frequently. Priority Application Instructions Departmental Contact Information Essential Job Functions Duty and Responsibility Financial Aid Systems Leadership & Strategy: Provides oversight and leadership for the financial aid management system, ensuring alignment with institutional priorities and enrollment strategies. Serves as Financial Aid Functional Lead, acting as liaison with Roosevelt’s Information Technology team and primary point of contact for financial aid systems processes, data, and reporting for external departments. Leads planning for the Ellucian Banner financial aid roadmap, including monitoring, testing, reporting, and coordination of software updates and upgrades. Collaborates with enrollment management leadership and systems leads in other enrollment units to align financial aid technology with broader university objectives. Percentage Of Time 35 Duty and Responsibility Data, Reporting & Compliance: Develops data‑driven insights and ensures accurate financial aid reporting for federal, state, and institutional compliance. Manages creation of reports and survey data by developing queries, producing reports for financial aid staff and administrative offices, and ensuring data integrity for federal, state, institutional, and audit reporting. Serves as a key resource for internal and external auditors by ensuring accuracy, consistency, and reliability of reported data. Percentage Of Time 25 Duty and Responsibility Technology Optimization, Automation & Process Improvement: Utilizes technology to enhance packaging, awarding, and student communications, optimizing system capabilities to improve efficiency and the student experience. Implements and supports automation strategies that streamline financial aid workflows and reduce manual processing. Directs system upgrades and process improvements to ensure seamless integration with campus technology and operational continuity. Percentage Of Time 20 Duty and Responsibility Technology Optimization, Automation & Process Improvement: · Utilizes technology to enhance packaging, awarding, and student communications, optimizing system capabilities to improve efficiency and the student experience. · Implements and supports automation strategies that streamline financial aid workflows and reduce manual processing. · Directs system upgrades and process improvements to ensure seamless integration with campus technology and operational continuity. Percentage Of Time 20 Duty and Responsibility New Initiatives & Innovation: Leads planning and implementation of new technology initiatives that enhance financial aid processing, service delivery, and regulatory compliance. Coordinates enhancements to online functionality and evaluates emerging tools to improve service and operational effectiveness. Percentage Of Time 10 Duty and Responsibility Training, Support & Cross ‑ Campus Collaboration: Provides training and guidance to financial aid staff on system usage and best practices. Proactively builds and maintains strong working relationships across the University to support continuous improvement of financial aid systems and programs. ** All responsibilities are carried out in accordance with the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act ( FERPA ), other applicable regulatory requirements, and professional standards. This description is not intended to be an exhaustive list of duties; other responsibilities logically associated with the position may be assigned. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned Bachelors degree? Yes No Do you have a minimum of five years of experience administering or supporting Ellucian Banner, including Ellucian BDMS, BCM, and Ellucian Action Line? Yes No Will you now or at any point in the future require employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) to legally work in the United States? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents 430 S. Michigan, Chicago, IL To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
