    "https://jobs.roosevelt.edu/postings/8895": {
      "title": "Clinical Administrative Coordinator- PA Program",
      "description": "Roosevelt University Employment Opportunities | Clinical Administrative Coordinator- PA Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Users Returning Users Clinical Administrative Coordinator- PA Program Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Clinical Administrative Coordinator- PA Program Category Administrative Position Number Posting Number S0001395 Location Schaumburg Open Date 09/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? No Job Type Full-Time Working Hours Position Summary Roosevelt University College of Health, Science and Pharmacy- Schaumburg seeks candidates for a full-time, non-exempt Clinical Administrative Coordinator to support the Physician Associate (PA) Studies program. The Clinical Administrative Coordinator plays a key role in the development of the PA program and supports the development and administration of the PA program’s clinical education infrastructure under the direction of the Program Director and designated clinical faculty. This is an in-person position that reports to the Program Director. Core duties include but are not limited to: clinical site development and affiliation agreements, clinical placement management, preceptor and student support, facilitate and manage communication with current students/faculty regarding all aspects of the PA program; support data collection and document retention needed for accreditation; plan and execute events and support events for the PA program, as well as led by other departments in the college. Roosevelt University offers many great benefits. Please review our benefits in further detail by clicking this link: https://rooseveltu.touchpointsonline.com/ The salary range for this position is $62,000-$66,000. Title IX Contact Information: Federal Title IX policy requires that all colleges and universities make known the contact information for the person responsible for coordinating its efforts to comply with Title IX regulations. At Roosevelt University, the Title IX Coordinator is Natasha Robinson. Her office is located in the Auditorium Building of the Chicago campus, 430 S. Michigan Avenue, AUD 476B. She can be reached at 312-281-3245 or TitleIX@roosevelt.edu. Do not contact this email address for inquiries about your job application; if you have questions, you may email hrquestions@roosevelt.edu . Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required Excellent organizational, communication (written and verbal), interpersonal skills and attention to detail. Ability to work efficiently and effectively with minimal supervision. Ability to maintain positive and professional demeanor with students, faculty and staff. Ability to manage data collection, report generation, and production. Ability to collaborate on accreditation preparation and support/execution of accreditation-related tasks/activities. Ability to work on event planning and event execution. Ability to exercise discretion and confidentiality. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (including Word, Excel, and Outlook), database systems (Salesforce, Exxat, etc), and video recording. Years of Experience Required 3 Required Education Bachelor's Degree Certification/Licensure Required Minimum Qualifications Please refer to Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities required section. Preferred Qualifications Experience in higher education, healthcare or program coordination; Proven record of organizational skill and positive and effective communication both written and verbal; Experience working with students. Equipment Operated Basic office equipment (laptop computer, copier/multi-function device, fax and telephone). Working Conditions Normal climate-controlled office environment is provided. There is a need to move between the office, classrooms and/or event space. Occasional bending, stooping, lifting, pushing and/or pulling is required (typically less than 45 pounds of weight or pressure). Regular use of desktop computer is required, calling for frequent hand/wrist movement and repetition. Occasional travel within the local or regional setting may be required. Priority Application Instructions Departmental Contact Information Essential Job Functions Duty and Responsibility Clinical Administrative Duties: Supports the recruitment and retention of sufficient clinical sites and preceptors across required clinical disciplines and settings Build partnerships with healthcare systems to support student placements Coordinate execution and tracking of clinical affiliation agreements Ensure agreements are active and compliant prior to student placement Develop and maintain student rotation schedules Maintain accurate tracking of sites, preceptors, and assignments Serve as a liaison for preceptors (onboarding, communication, engagement) Monitor student compliance with clinical requirements Track clinical data (hours, patient encounters, settings, lifespan exposure) Serve as a central point of contact for faculty, staff and students in the PA program Support accreditation reporting and program evaluation process Understand college and university operations and address inquiries and problems in an accurate and timely manner Manage student matriculation and enrollment records including those required for clinical experiences Oversee PA assessment data collection and document maintenance as required for programmatic improvement and accreditation compliance. Percentage Of Time 80 Duty and Responsibility Event Coordinator: Plan and execute events for the programs/college including but not limited to ceremonies, open houses, orientations; support events that are led by other offices in the college. Percentage Of Time 10 Duty and Responsibility Other duties as assigned. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have an earned Bachelors degree? Yes No Will you now or at any point in the future require employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) to legally work in the United States? Yes No This is a fully on-site position. Do you have the ability to be on campus 5 days a week? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents 430 S. Michigan, Chicago, IL To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.roosevelt.edu/postings/8887": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor for Biological, Physical and Health Sciences",
      "description": "Roosevelt University Employment Opportunities | Academic Advisor for Biological, Physical and Health Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Users Returning Users Academic Advisor for Biological, Physical and Health Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Academic Advisor for Biological, Physical and Health Sciences Category Administrative Position Number Posting Number S0001394 Location Hybrid - Chicago Open Date 09/09/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? No Job Type Full-Time Working Hours Position Summary Roosevelt University seeks an Academic Advisor to meet with continuing, new and prospective students in the Department of Biological, Physical and Health Sciences. This position will provide accurate, current curricular information on undergraduate programs in the department of BPHS ; assist in short-term and long-term academic program planning; refer students to other support services / units on campus; provide assistance with program changes (class drops and adds and major changes), and career plans; assist in recruitment and retention efforts which progresses our students toward graduation. This is a full-time, exempt position located on the Chicago campus. This position reports to the Director of Academic Advising. Some evening and weekend hours are required. Roosevelt University offers many great benefits. Please review our benefits in further detail by clicking this link: https://rooseveltu.touchpointsonline.com/ The salary range for this position is $50,000-$52,000. Title IX Contact Information: Federal Title IX policy requires that all colleges and universities make known the contact information for the person responsible for coordinating its efforts to comply with Title IX regulations. At Roosevelt University, the Title IX Coordinator is Natasha Robinson. Her office is located in the Auditorium Building of the Chicago campus, 430 S. Michigan Avenue, AUD 476B. She can be reached at 312-281-3245 or TitleIX@roosevelt.edu. Do not contact this email address for inquiries about your job application; if you have questions, you may email hrquestions@roosevelt.edu . Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required A minimum of 1 year of experience in a college environment working within student development or academic advising. Ability to use computerized student information systems and personal computing software. Proven ability to perform assigned administrative duties focused on supporting our advising, recruitment, and retention efforts. Excellent organizational, communication (written and verbal), interpersonal skills and attention to detail. Ability to exercise considerable judgment and discretion in establishing and maintaining good working relationships. Ability to demonstrate a commitment to service excellence by embodying Roosevelt’s core values, mission, and vision in every aspect of the role working with students, faculty, staff, and visitors. A positive and professional demeanor is a must. Demonstrated proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite including Word, Excel, and Outlook Years of Experience Required 1 Required Education Bachelor's Degree Certification/Licensure Required Minimum Qualifications Please refer to Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities required. Preferred Qualifications Masters degree preferred and 1 year of experience. Familiarity with Ellucian/Banner Equipment Operated Office equipment (desktop computer, office copier/ multifunction device and phone). Working Conditions Normal climate-controlled office environment is provided. Job is largely sedentary, but there is a need to move about the office and buildings frequently. Occasional bending, stooping, lifting, pushing and/or pulling is required (typically less than 10 pounds of weight or pressure). Regular use of desktop computer is required, calling for frequent hand/wrist movement and repetition. Moderate level of stress. Occasional travel within the local or regional setting may be required. Priority Application Instructions Departmental Contact Information Essential Job Functions Duty and Responsibility Provide accurate, current curricular information to students and prospective students on undergraduate programs in individual and group settings; assist in short-term and long-term academic program planning; provide information to faculty, staff, parents and others through workshops, orientations, and information sessions. Provide academic advising to specialized populations of students as deemed necessary. Percentage Of Time 60 Duty and Responsibility Serve as liaison, establish and develop effective relationships, create goals and plans for assessing goals with students, faculty, departmental heads, deans, and others, both on-and off-campus. Maintain key initiatives related to university systems. This technology includes and is not limited to EAB Navigate, Student Education Planning, Degree Audit and Ed Sights. Percentage Of Time 20 Duty and Responsibility Complete additional administrative duties, including preparation of reports on advisees and development of advising training materials, and supports faculty and staff in responding to student questions or issues. Exemplify the qualities of the service initiative C.A.R.E. by exhibiting the qualities of consistent, accessible, respectful and efficient service to all internal and external constituents. Percentage Of Time 15 Duty and Responsibility The Academic Advisor may be assigned additional related tasks in support of the department/University’s mission and goals. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have an earned Bachelor degree? yes no * Do you have a minimum of 1 year of experience in a college environment working with student development, academic advising theory, and knowledge of student support services available to college students? If so, please provide details of this experience. (Open Ended Question) Do you have the ability to use computerized student information systems and personal computing software? (Open Ended Question) Will you now or at any point in the future require employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) to legally work in the United States? Yes No This is a hybrid position. Do you have the ability to work on the Chicago campus 3 days per week and attend any other in-person events as required? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents 430 S. Michigan, Chicago, IL To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
