    "https://jobs.roosevelt.edu/postings/8635": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty, Sociology",
      "description": "Roosevelt University Employment Opportunities | Part-Time Faculty, Sociology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help New Users Returning Users Part-Time Faculty, Sociology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Rank Track Non-Tenure Track Position Title Part-Time Faculty, Sociology Category Adjunct Posting Number T000167 Location Chicago Open Date 01/22/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled? Yes Job Type Part-Time Working Hours Position Summary The College of Humanities, Education and Social Sciences at Roosevelt University invites applications for a part-time teaching position in Sociology. An M.A. in Sociology or related field is required, though some doctoral work is preferred. The successful candidate will teach 1-2 courses per academic semester. The primary teaching responsibility will be one Introduction to Sociology course and, if desired, a 200-level course in any of these topics: Juvenile Justice, Health and Inequality, or Social Issues. Applicants are expected to demonstrate excellence in teaching, be comfortable in and support a working environment that fosters diversity, use technology effectively in teaching, and be committed to the advancement of social justice. The current salary for this position is $3,982. Primary responsibilities include: · Providing instruction to undergraduate students · Teaching in multiple modalities: in-person, hybrid, and online asynchronous · Demonstrating proficiency with online teaching technologies such as Blackboard Ultra and Zoom · Engaging in department, college, and university service activities when appropriate Title IX Contact Information: Federal Title IX policy requires that all colleges and universities make known the contact information for the person responsible for coordinating its efforts to comply with Title IX regulations. At Roosevelt University, the Title IX Coordinator is Natasha 