nowledge, Skills and Abilities Required A Master’s Degree in Business, Recreation Management or closely aligned field. Experience managing sports venues Knowledge of and experience with Blackboard Ultra Learning Management System Years of Experience Required 1-2 years of prior experience teaching at the university level Required Education Masters Degree Certification/Licensure Required Minimum Qualifications See Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Required. Preferred Qualifications Professional Experience in the Sports Management field. Equipment Operated Basic office/classroom equipment (desktop computer, laptop, overhead projector, office copier). Working Conditions Available to teach F2F classes on Chicago campus. Normal climate-controlled office environment is provided. Job is largely sedentary, but there is a need to move about the office and buildings frequently. Occasional bending, stooping, lifting, pushing and/or pulling is required (typically less than 10 pound) Priority Application Instructions Departmental Contact Information Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a Master’s Degree in Business, Recreation Management or a closely aligned field? Yes No This is a on site position. Do you have the ability to be in person? Yes No Will you now or at any point in the future require employment visa sponsorship (e.g., H-1B) to legally work in the United States? Yes No Do you have 1-2 years of prior experience teaching at the university level? yes no Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Letter of Interest Optional Documents 430 S. Michigan, Chicago, IL To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
